{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/585344-revisit-2e-kith-and-seeming-from-durance","id":585344,"title":"Revisit: 2e Kith and Seeming from Durance","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-09T16:34:07-07:00","id":585344,"title":"Revisit: 2e Kith and Seeming from Durance","content":"Short form: the character spent twenty years (her time) playing through extended-setting versions of the laserdisc video games that were popular back in the 80s. She won her freedom by going through all the games perfectly in a long, marathon session, then got in the van of the last game's player character and drove off, out of her Keeper's Realm, into the Hedge, and finally back to Earth. In 1e, she's an Ogre (her Durance involved getting killed a lot, usually painfully), Bloodbrute kith (weaponise everything is extremely valuable in a Durance like that). But what might her 2e Kith and Seeming be?<br /> <br /> She was abducted because she played a perfect game of Dragon's Lair, then left the arcade while the sun and moon both shone upon the door (this is actually a fairly common thing), finding herself in a dark, overgrown wood, thick with brambles. Leaping, chattering death's-heads chased her into a cottage, keeping her trapped until after she drank Arcadian soda, ate Arcadian cheesies, and showered with Arcadian soap and shampoo. After the shower, she discovered her Earthside clothes were gone, replaced by Dirk's mail from Dragon's Lair. Her Keeper spoke out of empty air, saying that she was chosen to save a magic realm, and she didn't buy it. Not after those crazy skulls. So the Keeper put it to her plainly: Play or die, of thirst and hunger, over and over again. So, she played the games, from the inside, in expanded versions of the implied settings, for twenty subjective years (though that time includes &quot;vacations&quot; in a particular period in Time Gal).<br /> <br /> Karen basically earned her freedom by being boring; she got good enough at enough things that she could get through her adventures reliably, without getting killed or severely injured, and eventually said to the Keeper she knew only as a voice with no definite gender characteristics, &quot;Look. I've mastered these things, so there's no more fun you can get out of me. I do one last run, all of them, then I'm out of here. Except that this time, whatever I get in one adventure, I can keep. Through the others and after I'm done. I figure I've earned them. It's that, or I just stay here in the staging area. Your choice, voice.&quot; Given the choice between a satisfying end to a story or a tedious, long-drawn-out non-ending, the Keeper agreed to the deal, with some further negotiations to hammer out the details. At the end of Braindead 13, Karen drove out of Arcadia, and out of the Hedge, in Lance's van, seen in the final scene of that game; she chose the game order, putting that one last precisely so she could claim that van. Along with Thayer's pouch (a bag of holding) and the blood sword of Iscar from Thayer's Quest, Dragonfang, Dirk's armour and some treasure from Dragon's Lair, Space Ace' blaster, and Reika Kirishima's laser pistol from Time Gal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1184,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","user":"LadyLens","date":". 07-09-2015, 07:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T17:07:13-07:00","id":585388,"title":"","content":"Not sure about Kith, since we only know a rough 1/3rd of those. Seeming I'd go for Wizened, since she escaped by being really good at the games and by manipulating her Keeper, both feats of skill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T17:10:59-07:00","id":585391,"title":"","content":"For some reason, Wizened stuck out instantly. Fairest may have been a close second due to the perfecting nature, but.. i dont know if it thematically fits. As a Wizened, perhaps a Gameplayer with more physical contracts on the side, she could be both a gamer geek, good at the literal playing of games, and adapting skills from them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T20:23:13-07:00","id":585580,"title":"","content":"Well... Wizened would involve the character viewing her ability to play games as something empowering.<br /> <br /> After escaping, is she going to want to play video games from time to time to relax and reconnect with herself (aka use her Wizened Blessing), or is she going to never want to touch a controller again in her whole life because she's fed up with them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T00:07:20-07:00","id":585718,"title":"","content":"Elemental could also work. In giving up her trappings as a real person, she truly became a video game character--nothing but digital info, levels, button combos. She becomes the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T02:49:03-07:00","id":585805,"title":"","content":"I could <i>maybe</i> see a Beast interpretation... Civility and taboos aren't useful when you're playing the same few games alone for twenty years.<br /> <br /> Ogre still works. Toughen yourself up after dying horribly for the thousandth time. Stab, shoot, kill. Like the Wizened, it kinda depends on Karen's personality. Does the Blessing work? Would she have a tendency to default to violence?<br /> <br /> Darkling and Fairest don't seem to work at all, though.<br /> <br /> As for kith... I'd say pick one that's about toughness or is good at fighting, then re-skin it. Half being a video game character could make you the equivalent of a Manikin and let you ignore puny meatbag needs like eating and sleeping. Or perhaps Metalflesh. The ability to do lethal damage unarmed is sorta similar to Bloodbrute in a &quot;always be prepare for a fight&quot; kind of way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T06:20:25-07:00","id":585978,"title":"","content":"I don't think any of the current Kiths fit. I'd suggest spinning up a Galliant Kith, knight in shining armour basically, since you were transfromed into a hero; lots of Heroes really.<br /> <br /> Now for Seeming. I'd say either no-Seeming or perhaps possibly the Loyalist Seeming. Your charachter didn't escape, she was released. This might be the Seeming Dave's teased is coming in Dark Eras.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-10-2015, 09:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T10:47:17-07:00","id":586259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/585344-revisit-2e-kith-and-seeming-from-durance?p=585580#post585580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well... Wizened would involve the character viewing her ability to play games as something empowering.<br /> <br /> After escaping, is she going to want to play video games from time to time to relax and reconnect with herself (aka use her Wizened Blessing), or is she going to never want to touch a controller again in her whole life because she's fed up with them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Once she gets up to speed on modern gaming, I could see the more abstract games appealing to her. Recognizable characters would be a turnoff, and games like World of Warcraft would give her the horrors, for fairly obvious reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T23:08:40-07:00","id":586838,"title":"","content":"There were laserdisc video games? Rad.<br /> <br /> For Seeming, I think Wizened fits best. Although she hasn't literally incorporated the tools of her trade into herself, they've obviously become an important part of her identity and coping strategy, and her path to release obviously involved dedication to the craft of adventuring. Escaping via a bargain is still an escape, especially in Arcadia where reality is only what is agreed upon. Her Keeper may feel cheated, especially considering the way she cleverly selected the order of the games to give herself a getaway vehicle, and may very well send agents after her in spite of having agreed to let her go.<br /> <br /> As has been stated, the Seemings are meant to be fairly broad; the descriptions given for them outline archetypal members of the Seeming, but it's more &quot;pick the one that sounds closest to your concept&quot; than &quot;you must fit cookie cutter!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 07-11-2015, 02:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T04:40:24-07:00","id":586968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/585344-revisit-2e-kith-and-seeming-from-durance?p=586259#post586259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Recognizable characters would be a turnoff, and games like World of Warcraft would give her the horrors, for fairly obvious reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I figured. In which case I'd tend to say Elemental or Ogre.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T11:48:48-07:00","id":588339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/585344-revisit-2e-kith-and-seeming-from-durance?p=586838#post586838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There were laserdisc video games? Rad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes there were. And yes they were. Here's a play through of the first LD game to hit the arcades: Dragon's Lair. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://youtu.be/i6em4GRiRY0\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://youtu.be/i6em4GRiRY0\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://youtu.be/i6em4GRiRY0\" target=\"_blank\"> http://youtu.be/i6em4GRiRY0 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T17:10:49-07:00","id":588604,"title":"","content":"I'm actually familiar with Dragon's Lair and Space Ace; the town I live in has an old seaside amusement park that still has several excellent arcades. I actually worked there a couple of summers. I didn't realize, however, that those games ran on Laserdisc. <br /> <br /> A friend of mine actually got a Laserdisc player recently; somebody in his neighborhood was giving it away for free. It's a neat piece of funky old technology, but I can kind of see why it didn't catch on. It appears that you actually have to flip the disc over partway through basically any feature-length movie. My friend's player can read both sides, but it still interrupts the movie while it switches, which is less than ideal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T13:50:33-07:00","id":589506,"title":"","content":"Not to mention the sharpness of the image was only slightly superior to Betamax, and the discs were very expensive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}